schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Silvi verifies trees and pays planters directly, with no middlemen"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Once a planted tree is verified (via phone photo, AI check, and
    community review), Silvi Protocol automatically sends payment (in cUSD or
    USDC) directly to the planter's wallet, with no middlemen and no delays,
    on a fully transparent, unchangeable blockchain record.
  evidence: >-
    Asserted throughout the article's "What is Silvi Protocol," "Why Does
    This Matter," and "How It Works" sections; no independent audit, technical
    documentation, or third-party account is cited in this source.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/silvi-protocol.md
  interpretation: >-
    Functions as the article's core value proposition: technology replacing
    trust intermediaries in ecological-impact funding.
  uncertainty: >-
    Single-sourced promotional playbook (no listed sources per frontmatter
    `sources: []`); payment reliability, AI-verification accuracy, and
    "permanent record that anyone can verify" claims are not independently
    confirmed here. High-risk as an ecological/MRV + payment claim about a
    named third-party protocol — should be corroborated against Silvi's own
    technical docs/audits before any public-facing reuse.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  high_risk: true
  public_use: not-public-yet
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/silvi-protocol.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
